**Day 19: Advanced SQL Querying with Complex Joins and Subqueries**  

**Topic:**  
Mastering complex SQL queries by combining JOINs, subqueries, aggregates, and views to solve multi-step problems efficiently.  

**Learning Objectives:**  
• Understand how to construct multi-step queries using JOINs and subqueries  
• Apply aggregate functions (COUNT, SUM, AVG) within complex queries  
• Optimize query performance using views and temporary tables  
• Solve real-world database problems with structured SQL logic  

**Activities / Deliverables:**  
• Solve 10 real-world SQL problems involving JOINs, subqueries, and aggregates  
• Peer review and discuss alternative solutions for optimization  
• Practice writing and debugging queries in MySQL Workbench  

**Important Concepts:**  
• **JOINs (INNER, LEFT, RIGHT, FULL)** – Combining data from multiple tables  
• **Subqueries** – Nesting queries for filtering or calculations  
• **Aggregate Functions** – Summarizing data (COUNT, SUM, AVG, GROUP BY)  
• **Views** – Creating reusable virtual tables for complex queries  

**SQL Syntax / Commands:**  
• `SELECT ... FROM table1 JOIN table2 ON ...`  
• `SELECT ... WHERE column IN (SELECT ...)`  
• `CREATE VIEW view_name AS SELECT ...`  
• `GROUP BY ... HAVING aggregate_condition`  

**Real-world Use Cases:**  
• Generating sales reports with aggregated revenue by region  
• Analyzing customer purchase history with nested queries  
• Optimizing query performance for large datasets using views  

**Tools / Tech:**  
• **MySQL 8** – Database management system  
• **MySQL Workbench** – GUI for query development and execution  

**Summary:**  
Today focused on advanced SQL techniques, combining JOINs, subqueries, and aggregates to solve complex problems. Hands-on practice with real-world scenarios reinforced query optimization and logical structuring. Peer discussions provided alternative approaches to problem-solving.  

